(7313621, 1140549, 100393, '<td valign="top">An interesting scene, but I don''t believe you''ve done it justice. I know who shot this and I also know that your work is normally much more engaging than this. I know you will tell me this is absolutely level but the impression to a viewer''s brain is that it needs righting. Images have audiences and their perception is as important as your intent when it comes to the forming of their vote.<br/> <br/>Those two trees are disappearing into the hillside beyond doesn''t work for me, and a low tonal level is set a little high for me - there is more shadow than there needs to be. I see few patches of true black, but too much just above the black point.<br/> <br/>What was your workflow? Did you apply curves? <br/> <br/>I think you''ve done a great job with the highlights, but it isn''t matched by the shadow work.<br/> <br/>Having said all that, I think you''ll get a bit more than your estimate. 5.65 perhaps?<br/> <br/>(I''ve looked on three monitors - granted only one allowed me to differentiate between the last two black blocks on the scale, but it didn''t help with my appreciation of the image).<br/> <br/>Perhaps it just a really hard scene to capture - I do believe that.</td>', 'An interesting scene, but I don''t believe you''ve done it justice. I know who shot this and I also know that your work is normally much more engaging than this. I know you will tell me this is absolutely level but the impression to a viewer''s brain is that it needs righting. Images have audiences and their perception is as important as your intent when it comes to the forming of their vote. Those two trees are disappearing into the hillside beyond doesn''t work for me, and a low tonal level is set a little high for me - there is more shadow than there needs to be. I see few patches of true black, but too much just above the black point. What was your workflow? Did you apply curves?  I think you''ve done a great job with the highlights, but it isn''t matched by the shadow work. Having said all that, I think you''ll get a bit more than your estimate. 5.65 perhaps? (I''ve looked on three monitors - granted only one allowed me to differentiate between the last two black blocks on the scale, but it didn''t help with my appreciation of the image). Perhaps it just a really hard scene to capture - I do believe that.', '2015-02-07 12:12:59.000000', NULL, 1),
(7313622, 1140719, 50695, '<td valign="top">Your guess seems right to me. 5.2</td>', 'Your guess seems right to me. 5.2', '2015-02-07 12:16:32.000000', NULL, 1),
(7313623, 1140238, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like the shadows and the almost absurd math you''re making me to. I think DPC will give you a 3.4</td>', 'I like the shadows and the almost absurd math you''re making me to. I think DPC will give you a 3.4', '2015-02-07 12:19:02.000000', NULL, 1),
(7313659, 1140719, 100393, '<td valign="top">I think this might do a bit better than 5.2 but it looks a bit over sharpened to me. The blue light that seems to be reflected is curious. I do like the sprouting greenery . More like 5.7 I think.</td>', 'I think this might do a bit better than 5.2 but it looks a bit over sharpened to me. The blue light that seems to be reflected is curious. I do like the sprouting greenery . More like 5.7 I think.', '2015-02-07 14:30:29.000000', NULL, 1),
(7313660, 1140293, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is well made. I really like the scene and you have captured in well. I predict more for you - 5.9?</td>', 'This is well made. I really like the scene and you have captured in well. I predict more for you - 5.9?', '2015-02-07 14:32:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(7313664, 1140232, 100393, '<td valign="top">I think that your guess is closer than your wish. The bird has quite an eclectic placement in the frame that I quite enjoy but the lack of detail in most of the wing parts, the noise and the dust spot  are likely to hurt your score I think. Consequently I think you may be around the 5.1 mark.</td>', 'I think that your guess is closer than your wish. The bird has quite an eclectic placement in the frame that I quite enjoy but the lack of detail in most of the wing parts, the noise and the dust spot  are likely to hurt your score I think. Consequently I think you may be around the 5.1 mark.', '2015-02-07 14:46:13.000000', NULL, 1),
(7313667, 1140705, 100393, '<td valign="top">This is a well constructed high contrast macro - it''s not an image that does much for me but I can appreciate the care that has been taken and the integrity of the final image. I think you''ll do a little better - 5.7?</td>', 'This is a well constructed high contrast macro - it''s not an image that does much for me but I can appreciate the care that has been taken and the integrity of the final image. I think you''ll do a little better - 5.7?', '2015-02-07 14:49:38.000000', NULL, 1),
(7313737, 1140269, 97225, '<td valign="top">5. The composition is fine, the tones a bit - well, muddy. Maybe if I were a four year old in gumboots this would excite me a bit more.</td>', '5. The composition is fine, the tones a bit - well, muddy. Maybe if I were a four year old in gumboots this would excite me a bit more.', '2015-02-07 16:44:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(7313776, 1140645, 115814, '<td valign="top">I gave it a seven. Guessing a 6.4.</td>', 'I gave it a seven. Guessing a 6.4.', '2015-02-07 16:56:49.000000', NULL, 1),
